<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orchies</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orchies is a small town in the Nord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lille">Lille</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douai">Douai</a>. With Lille and Douai it formed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walloon-flanders">Walloon Flanders</a>, the French-speaking south of the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, and was transferred with them to the French crown in 1312 after the Franco-Flemish wars. It returned to Flanders in 1369 and became French again through the conquests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> in 1667–1668.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orchies.jpg" alt="Orchies" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JackyM59 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_d%27Orchies_et_son_beffroi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
